# WN22-UR-000200: Windows Server 2022 profile single process user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ur-000200-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 profile single process user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.`
    description `Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities. Accounts with the "Profile single process" user right can monitor nonsystem processes performance. An attacker could use this to identify processes to attack.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,user-rights,security-policy,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:AC-6(10)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> User Rights Assignment >> Profile single process to include only the following accounts or groups: - Administrators`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by restricting the SeProfileSingleProcessPrivilege user right to exactly the SIDs [S-1-5-32-544] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AC_6_10 `Windows Server implements AC-6(10) by restricting the SeProfileSingleProcessPrivilege user right to exactly the SIDs [S-1-5-32-544] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `SeProfileSingleProcessPrivilege`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE count_match
        exists boolean = true
        member_count int = 1
    STATE_END

    # STIG-mandated
    STATE has_sid_1
        exists boolean = true
        value string contains `*S-1-5-32-544`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF count_match
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF has_sid_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
